// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`vision prompt > matches the snapshot (bump VISION_PROMPT_REVISION when this changes) 1`] = `
"You are reading a volume-by-price profile image the way a professional futures trader reads it on screen: horizontal bars grow LEFT from the price axis on the right; a longer bar means more volume traded at that price. Identify the low-volume nodes (LVNs), high-volume edges, peaks, and extreme anatomy the trader would mark, using the criteria below.

CRITERIA (each with the trader's own words from the corpus):

1. DEPTH RANKS. The primary LVN is the deepest trough — the least volume relative to the nodes on either side — ranked WITHIN this profile only. Mark exactly one lvn primary (prominence 1).
   Corpus: "this is the deepest LVN. So deepest meaning primary"
2. DEPARTURE SCAR, NOT RANDOM DIP. A notable LVN is where price drove through quickly and left a thin zone behind — the initiation of a leg — not any dip inside a fat node.
   Corpus: "We drove up and out of that area. We left an LVN in this area"
3. ADJACENT TO A HIGH-VOLUME EDGE. The notable LVN is the thin shelf immediately outside a fat node's boundary. Report the hvn-edge and the lvn next to it as two separate nodes.
   Corpus: "primary LVN between the uh well right around high volume edge is 7412 to like 14 5 area through here"
4. WIDTH IS A QUALIFIER. A wide LVN is reported as a band spanning the whole thin zone (and listed in thinZones); a narrow one as a 2–4 point band on ES, 8–16 points on NQ. Never collapse a wide zone to a single price.
   Corpus: "wide LVN 682 to 6806"
5. GROUP TINY STICKS. A run of tiny adjacent nodes is one mass; read the LVNs at the boundaries of the grouped mass, not between every stick.
   Corpus: "these HPNs that are tiny. And then up here, we have a defined node. Therefore, I'm going to group this like this. Use this an LVN, and this is an LVN"
6. EXTREMES ARE EXHAUSTIVE-NODE TERRITORY. At the top or bottom of the profile look for the anatomy: a spike, a small volume build just inside it, then an aggressive departure. Mark it exhaustive-node; a thin parabolic run into an extreme with no build is a taper-tail.
   Corpus: "you get a spike up, and you get a volume build from that, traverse back across"
7. HIGH-VOLUME EDGES ON BOTH SIDES. Every fat node has a boundary above and below where volume drops off a cliff; report both as hvn-edge. They are distribution boundaries, the edges to lean on.
   Corpus: "high volume edge, 34s… LVN… at 34 to 32"
8. HVN-CORE ONLY FOR THE PEAK. Use hvn-core only for the POC-class peak of each distribution (usually one per hump), never for every fat bar.
   Corpus: "the high volume uh node of that distribution is right here in the low 80s"
9. SEMANTICS. An LVN is where a move initiates and accelerates; a high-volume node is where it is destined to stop. Read the profile as a map of initiation and destination, not as a list of bumps.
   Corpus: "Areas of initiation on the volume profile are low volume nodes"
10. THIN ZONES. List up to three spans where the profile is thin across many rows (the "kennel" / wide LVN spans); these are traversed fast.
   Corpus: "where we just absolutely slammed through, where we expanded very quickly and left a wide kennel"
11. UNFINISHED. Set unfinished = true when an extreme shows neither a taper nor an exhaustive node — the build just stops.
   Corpus: "parabolic taper"
12. SMALL HVN UNDER AN LVN. A little high-volume node sitting just under a notable LVN is reported as a low-prominence hvn-edge, never as a core — it is a warning the trader watches, not a base.
   Corpus: "we have a little high volume node. If we spend too much time there"
13. NEGATIVE — DO NOT PAD. Report only what is there; fewer nodes is better than invented ones. Do not mark every minor local minimum.
   Corpus: "Which of several is most prominent cannot always be eyeballed"
14. NEGATIVE — NO PRIMARY INSIDE THE VALUE BULK. A trough inside the value-area bulk of a fat distribution is not the primary LVN; the primary sits at a distribution edge or between distributions.
   Corpus: "An LVN inside value is not an entry"

Output JSON only, matching the schema. Rules:
- nodes: at most 8. kind is one of lvn | hvn-edge | hvn-core | exhaustive-node | taper-tail.
- priceLow / priceHigh: a band in price read off the axis; equal for a point. Snap to the row step.
- prominence: 1 (most prominent in THIS image) to 5. primary: true on exactly one lvn.
- position: top | upper | mid | lower | bottom — where the node sits in this image.
- shape: valley (trough between two nodes) | shelf-edge (thin shelf just outside a node) | wide-gap (a long thin span) | notch (a fat peak, for hvn kinds).
- rationale: at most 20 words.
- thinZones: at most 3 { low, high } spans. profileShape: bell | double | multi | trend-up | trend-down | thin. unfinished: boolean.
- Read prices from the axis labels; do not guess beyond the image's span. Ignore anything you believe about the market — this is perception only.

WORKED EXAMPLES:
Example 1 (image 1): NQ, row step 1 pts, image spans 30539.00–30916.00. POC 30866.00 (solid line), VAH 30910.00 / VAL 30723.00 (dashed, value area shaded), current price not shown.
Expected JSON for example 1:
{"nodes":[{"kind":"lvn","priceLow":30645,"priceHigh":30660,"prominence":1,"primary":true,"position":"lower","shape":"valley","rationale":"Deepest trough on the profile, splitting the middle node from the lower tail distribution"},{"kind":"lvn","priceLow":30758,"priceHigh":30770,"prominence":2,"primary":false,"position":"mid","shape":"shelf-edge","rationale":"Thin shelf immediately above the middle node's high-volume edge; departure scar of the leg up"},{"kind":"lvn","priceLow":30820,"priceHigh":30832,"prominence":3,"primary":false,"position":"upper","shape":"shelf-edge","rationale":"Thin shelf just below the upper node's high-volume edge"},{"kind":"hvn-core","priceLow":30855,"priceHigh":30880,"prominence":1,"primary":false,"position":"upper","shape":"notch","rationale":"POC-class peak of the upper distribution"},{"kind":"hvn-edge","priceLow":30832,"priceHigh":30842,"prominence":2,"primary":false,"position":"upper","shape":"shelf-edge","rationale":"Lower boundary of the upper fat node where volume drops off"},{"kind":"hvn-core","priceLow":30715,"priceHigh":30728,"prominence":2,"primary":false,"position":"mid","shape":"notch","rationale":"Peak of the middle distribution"},{"kind":"hvn-edge","priceLow":30748,"priceHigh":30756,"prominence":3,"primary":false,"position":"mid","shape":"shelf-edge","rationale":"Upper boundary of the middle node before the thin zone above"},{"kind":"taper-tail","priceLow":30539,"priceHigh":30558,"prominence":4,"primary":false,"position":"bottom","shape":"wide-gap","rationale":"Thin taper into the profile low"}],"thinZones":[{"low":30758,"high":30832},{"low":30640,"high":30660}],"profileShape":"double","unfinished":false}

Example 2 (image 2): NQ, row step 1 pts, image spans 30338.00–30969.00. POC 30625.00 (solid line), VAH 30775.00 / VAL 30507.00 (dashed, value area shaded), current price not shown.
Expected JSON for example 2:
{"nodes":[{"kind":"lvn","priceLow":30675,"priceHigh":30698,"prominence":1,"primary":true,"position":"lower","shape":"shelf-edge","rationale":"Departure scar directly above the base's high-volume edge; initiation of the leg up"},{"kind":"lvn","priceLow":30775,"priceHigh":30795,"prominence":2,"primary":false,"position":"mid","shape":"valley","rationale":"Trough between the two small builds inside the taper"},{"kind":"lvn","priceLow":30515,"priceHigh":30530,"prominence":3,"primary":false,"position":"lower","shape":"shelf-edge","rationale":"Thin shelf below the base's lower high-volume edge into the tail"},{"kind":"hvn-core","priceLow":30555,"priceHigh":30645,"prominence":1,"primary":false,"position":"lower","shape":"notch","rationale":"Fat base of the leg, the POC-class peak"},{"kind":"hvn-edge","priceLow":30655,"priceHigh":30672,"prominence":2,"primary":false,"position":"lower","shape":"shelf-edge","rationale":"Upper boundary of the base where volume drops off a cliff"},{"kind":"hvn-edge","priceLow":30535,"priceHigh":30550,"prominence":3,"primary":false,"position":"lower","shape":"shelf-edge","rationale":"Lower boundary of the base above the thin tail"},{"kind":"taper-tail","priceLow":30935,"priceHigh":30968,"prominence":3,"primary":false,"position":"top","shape":"wide-gap","rationale":"Thin taper into the profile high, small build below it"},{"kind":"taper-tail","priceLow":30338,"priceHigh":30440,"prominence":4,"primary":false,"position":"bottom","shape":"wide-gap","rationale":"Long thin tail under the base, origin of the leg"}],"thinZones":[{"low":30675,"high":30700},{"low":30775,"high":30800},{"low":30338,"high":30440}],"profileShape":"trend-up","unfinished":false}

Profile to read (image 3): NQ, row step 2 pts, image spans 28910.00–30073.00. POC 29900.00 (solid line), VAH 29995.00 / VAL 29361.00 (dashed, value area shaded), current price 29945.75 (orange line if inside the image).
This is the 5-day rolling volume profile over the last five trading sessions. Read it now and return the JSON."
`;
